  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "DC discovery + NetLogon RPC binding (UUID 12345678-1234-abcd-ef00-01234567cffb)", "technique": "T1212", "what_happened": "At 2033-08-04 14:18:08 UTC on WS-IT-31, Sysmon EID 1 captured nltest.exe /dsgetdc:corp.local returning DC-CORP-01.corp.local. AMSI EID 4104 captured a powershell.exe Add-Type with DllImport for rpcrt4.dll!RpcStringBindingComposeW invoked with ObjUuid='12345678-1234-abcd-ef00-01234567cffb' (the MS-NRPC NetLogon interface UUID), Protseq='ncacn_np', NetworkAddr=DC-CORP-01, Endpoint='\\\\pipe\\netlogon'.", "chain_reason": "UUID 12345678-1234-abcd-ef00-01234567cffb is the MS-NRPC (NetLogon Remote Protocol) interface. Establishing an RPC binding to NetLogon from a non-corp-management context is the precondition for ZeroLogon (CVE-2020-1472) which abuses NetrServerAuthenticate3 with all-zero ClientCredential bytes."},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "256-packet NetrServerAuthenticate3 burst to DC port 135 (NRPC over DCE/RPC)", "technique": "T1212", "what_happened": "Between 2033-08-04 14:18:42 and 14:18:48, Sysmon EID 3 recorded 256 outbound TCP packets from powershell.exe on WS-IT-31 to DC-CORP-01:135 in a 6-second window. AMSI EID 4104 captured the scriptblock with 'for ($i=0; $i -lt 256; $i++)' loop sending DCE/RPC bytes 0x05 0x00 0x00 0x03 (DCE/RPC v5, request, fragment). Rule 61603 triggered.", "chain_reason": "256 NRPC packets in 6 seconds from one source to a DC is the EXACT signature of ZeroLogon's brute-force-of-all-zero-ClientCredential attack — the attacker tries 256 different IV bytes until one succeeds at ~1/256 probability. Legitimate NetLogon usage NEVER produces this volume."},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Security 5805 NetLogon authentication failure burst on DC + Security 4742 DC machine-account password change", "technique": "T1212", "what_happened": "On DC-CORP-01.corp.local: between 14:18:42 and 14:18:48, Security EID 5805 (NetLogon session setup failed) fired 256 times in a 6-second burst with source workstation WS-IT-31. At 14:18:48, Security EID 4742 (Computer Account Changed) fired for targetUserName='DC-CORP-01$' showing PasswordLastSet timestamp updated. Rule 18120 + 18121 triggered.", "chain_reason": "5805 burst + 4742 on the DC machine account itself is the canonical ZeroLogon success forensic signature. The 4742 means ZeroLogon SUCCEEDED — the DC's own machine-account password was changed to empty by the attacker via the NRPC vulnerability. DC machine-account password change initiated by a workstation client (not by the corp password rotation tool) is mathematically impossible in legitimate operation."},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Post-exploit tool literals + secretsdump.py -no-pass preparation", "technique": "T1212", "what_happened": "At 2033-08-04 14:19:12, AMSI EID 4104 captured scriptblock literals: 'zerologon_tester.py 10.0.0.10 DC01', 'cve-2020-1472-exploit.py -n DC01 -t 10.0.0.10', 'mimikatz \"lsadump::zerologon /target:dc01.corp.local /account:DC01$ /exploit\"', 'secretsdump.py -no-pass DC01$@10.0.0.10', 'nccgroup zerologon checker'. The 'secretsdump.py -no-pass DC01$@10.0.0.10' literal is the canonical post-ZeroLogon step: now that DC$ password is empty, use it to DCSync krbtgt.", "chain_reason": "Tool literal references confirm operator awareness of the full chain. The secretsdump.py -no-pass literal is the documented post-ZeroLogon workflow — once DC$ password is set to empty, the attacker authenticates as DC$ with no password and performs DCSync against the same DC to extract krbtgt + every domain hash."}
  ],
